; Leg DS -- the host RECEIVES.  The Victor SENDS TRANS.DAT at 38400 with
; --rtscts.  START THIS FIRST: the Victor is the initiator.
;
; THE CTS GATE.  --rtscts makes v9k_ser_put() require RR0 CTS before every
; byte it writes.  SS16v read cts=1 on this cable in both legs with the host
; holding RTS asserted, so this should transfer -- and this leg is here
; because if it does not, the failure is TOTAL SILENCE rather than a slow
; or corrupt transfer, and that is the failure the FLO_NONE default exists
; to avoid.  Run it early so a wedge is diagnosed before the sitting is
; spent, and do not debug it at the bench: record it and stop this arm.
;
; The host runs "set flow rts/cts" here, which means it may drop ITS RTS --
; so this also tests that we notice and resume, not just that we start.
;
; PASS:  byte-exact, stuck=0, cps in leg CC's band (~1,4xx).
; FAIL:  no packets at all in s16ajDS.pkt -> CTS is not asserted here, and
;        SS16v's reading was of something else.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set flow rts/cts
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16ajDS.pkt
receive gotds.dat
statistics
